# Testing

## Setup
- Jest + React Testing Library; tests in `__tests__/` next to source or in `*.test.ts(x)`.
- Run: `npm test` (from gospel-admin). No `--run` flag for Jest.

## Patterns
- Use `render()`, `screen`, `waitFor`, `userEvent` from RTL; avoid testing implementation details.
- Mock `fetch` or external APIs when testing components that load data (e.g. ScriptureModal, ComaModal).
- For components that use theme or modal context, mock the context or provider (e.g. `ThemeContext`, `AlertModalContext`) when they cause act() warnings or missing providers.

## Snapshots
- Prefer asserting on behavior and visible text over snapshot tests. If snapshots are used, update them only when the intended output changes.

## API route tests
- Use `NextRequest` and call the exported handler; assert on `NextResponse` status and JSON body.
